<title>SINGAPORE: Pacific Carriers H1 net down 5 pct.</title>
<headline>Pacific Carriers H1 net down 5 pct.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1996-09-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six months to June 30, 1996</p>
<p>			 (in millions of S$ unless stated)</p>
<p>    Net profit			   13.69   vs   14.45</p>
<p>    Group shr (cents)		   4.56   vs    4.82</p>
<p>    Turnover			     63.46   vs   62.30</p>
<p>    Other income incl. interest     0.87   vs    1.48</p>
<p>    Interest (expense)		  nil    vs    0.40</p>
<p>    Depreciation (expense)	    6.53   vs    8.14</p>
<p>    Profits from associates	   6.43   vs    9.65</p>
<p>    Pre-tax profit			9.20   vs    5.66</p>
<p>    Tax				     1.90   vs    1.00</p>
<p>    Minorities		   (loss) 0.05   vs    0.14 (gain)</p>
<p>    Extraordinaries		     nil    vs   14.04 (gain)</p>
<p>Note - Pacific Carriers Ltd has shipowning, chartering and freight trading interests.</p>
<p>-- Singapore newsroom (65 8703199)</p>
</text>
